From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emuTOS-MCD <darekadumon@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 03:39:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 162/190] Sega CD: boot from A:, the ROM system disk, not C:

DEFAULT_BOOTDEV is C: because on an ST the hard disk is where a system
lives. Here C: is a save chip on whatever cartridge happens to be in
the slot -- it may be absent, it may hold somebody else's game saves,
and FORMATC.PRG exists precisely so it can be wiped. A: is the
ROM-resident system disk: always there, always ours, and not changed by
anything the user does.

It is not only tidiness. The boot drive is where the desktop looks for
its own files: app_rdicon() and read_inf_file() both adjust their
filename by G.g_stdrv, which is dos_gdrv() at desktop start, which is
whatever Dsetdrv(bootdev) made current. So EMUDESK.INF and EMUICON.RSC
were being looked for on the cartridge and quietly not found, which is
not a failure any message reports -- the desktop just builds a default
INF and uses the built-in icons, exactly as it would on a machine that
had never been given any.

blkdev.h now takes a prior definition so the machine can say.
---
 bios/blkdev.h    |  2 ++
 include/config.h | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/bios/blkdev.h b/bios/blkdev.h
index bdbc470..8dadbe9 100644
--- a/bios/blkdev.h
+++ b/bios/blkdev.h
@@ -37,7 +37,9 @@
 
 #define FLOPPY_BOOTDEV      0   /* i.e. A: */
 #define HARDDISK_BOOTDEV    2   /* i.e. C: */
+#ifndef DEFAULT_BOOTDEV
 #define DEFAULT_BOOTDEV     HARDDISK_BOOTDEV
+#endif
 
 /* Original FAT12 bootsector */
 struct bs {
diff --git a/include/config.h b/include/config.h
index aa8bcf6..e8f7fa1 100644
--- a/include/config.h
+++ b/include/config.h
@@ -629,6 +629,23 @@
     * own bus, alongside ACSI, SCSI, IDE and SD. */
 #  define CONF_WITH_SEGACD_CD 1
 # endif
+# ifndef DEFAULT_BOOTDEV
+   /* A:, and not C:.
+    *
+    * DEFAULT_BOOTDEV is C: because on an ST the hard disk is where a
+    * system lives. Here C: is a save chip on whatever cartridge is in
+    * the slot -- it may be absent, it may hold somebody else's game
+    * saves, and FORMATC.PRG exists precisely so it can be wiped. A: is
+    * the ROM-resident system disk: always there, always ours, never
+    * changed by anything the user does.
+    *
+    * It is not only tidiness. The boot drive is where the desktop looks
+    * for EMUDESK.INF and EMUICON.RSC -- app_rdicon() and
+    * read_inf_file() both adjust their filename by G.g_stdrv -- so with
+    * C: as the boot drive the icons this machine ships were being
+    * looked for on the cartridge and quietly not found. */
+#  define DEFAULT_BOOTDEV 0
+# endif
 # ifndef CONF_WITH_READ_INF
 #  define CONF_WITH_READ_INF 0
 # endif
